BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC State Gregg Museum of Art & Design
CATEGORIES:Lectures and Talks,Community Events,Exhibitions,Films,Student Li
 fe,High-Impact Experiences
DESCRIPTION:Join the Gregg Museum of Art & Design for a free screening of t
 he documentary Repatriation to Restoration and a conversation about repatri
 ation. We invite you to reflect on the responsibility museums hold in retur
 ning sacred objects to their rightful communities. Filmmakers Ben West and 
 Yancey Burns of the Rena Flying Coyote Collective explore that responsibili
 ty in the film. The Rena Flying Coyote Collective is a nonprofit dedicated 
 to sharing Indigenous stories through film\, television and the arts.\n\nFo
 llowing the screening\, Nancy Chavis\, director of the Museum of the Southe
 ast American Indian at the University of North Carolina at Pembroke\, will 
 join West and Burns for a brief discussion about the film and a Q&A with th
 e audience. Registration is required to attend the screening.
DTEND:20260527T230000Z
DTSTAMP:20260501T040932Z
DTSTART:20260527T213000Z
GEO:35.784762;-78.661636
LOCATION:Gregg Museum of Art & Design\, Lobby 
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Film Screening: Repatriation to Restoration
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52523740428887
URL:https://calendar.ncsu.edu/event/film-screening-artist-talk
END:VEVENT
